  "why": "A composite slab uses profiled steel decking as permanent formwork acting with the concrete topping, so there is no traditional carpentry — the trades are deck laying, shear-stud welding, light mesh reinforcement and topping concrete; each is a separate crew and the deck plus studs replace the soffit form entirely.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Steel or composite frame already erected",
    "Total slab ~120–140 mm, net concrete ≈0.10 m3/m2",
    "Single 8 hr/day shift",
    "Through-deck stud welding",
    "Light mesh + local trench bars only"
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "Abnormal congestion",
    "Rework/deck re-laying",
    "Structural steel beams/frame (separate item)",
    "Edge trims/closures beyond the allowance"
